From: BC-250 LLM package maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ac: enable repaired GFX1013 compute queues and ACE workaround

Fedora 44 Mesa 26.2.4 already contains the GFX1013 GFX10.1 IP-version
correction added upstream in Mesa 26.2.1, so do not carry that obsolete
hunk here.

The package-owned V33 kernel profile repairs the GFX1013 compute-queue
lifecycle.  For the matching private RADV only:

- stop rejecting the GFX1013 compute IP when compute rings are exposed;
- apply the existing Iceland/Tonga async-compute threadgroup workaround to
  GFX1013, matching the behavior proven by the accepted BC-250 profile.

This patch is intentionally scoped to the private package RADV.  Do not use
it with the stock kernel path.

--- a/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
+++ b/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
@@ -519,9 +519,4 @@
-   /* GFX1013 is known to have broken compute queue */
-   if (device_info.family == FAMILY_NV && ASICREV_IS(device_info.external_rev, GFX1013)) {
-      info->ip[AMD_IP_COMPUTE].num_queues = 0;
-   }
-
    /* Set dword padding minus 1. */
    info->ip[AMD_IP_GFX].ib_pad_dw_mask = 0x7;
    info->ip[AMD_IP_COMPUTE].ib_pad_dw_mask = 0x7;
    info->ip[AMD_IP_SDMA].ib_pad_dw_mask = 0xf;
@@ -1015,7 +1010,8 @@ void ac_fill_bug_info(struct radeon_info *info)
     * dimension mode.
     */
    info->has_async_compute_threadgroup_bug = info->family == CHIP_ICELAND ||
-                                             info->family == CHIP_TONGA;
+                                             info->family == CHIP_TONGA ||
+                                             info->family == CHIP_GFX1013;
 
    /* GFX7 CP requires 32 bytes alignment for the indirect buffer arguments on
     * the compute queue.
